---
title: Pumpkin Pie Brownies
course: Dessert
tags: 
- brownies
- vegan
- tested with gf flour
source: Vegan Cookies Invade Your Cookie Jar
servings: 8 brownies
---

Preheat oven to 350. Grease a #9-inch springform pan{}, lined with parchment paper. 

== for the Brownie Layer ==
Melt the @bittersweet chocolate{4%ounches}(melted).

In a #large mixing bowl{}, mix together the @canned pumpkin{1%cup}, @sugar{1/2%cup}, @vegetable oil{1/4%cup}, and @vanilla{1%tsp}. Sift in the @all-purpose flour{3/4%cup}, @cocoa powder{1/4%cup}, @tapioca flour{1%tbsp}(or arrowroot powder or cornstarch), @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} and stir to combiine, then mix in the melted chocolate.

== for the Pumpkin Layer ==

Mix the @canned pumpkin{3/4%cup}, @tapioca flour{2%tbsp}(or arrowroot powder or cornstarch), @plant based milk{1/2%cup}, @pure vanilla extract{1%tsp}, @ground ginger{1/4%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/4%tsp}, @ground nutmeg{a pinch}, and @ground allspice{a pinch} in a #large mixing bowl{} and stir until thoroughly combined.

== to Assemble ==

Use a #spatula{} to spread the brownie layer mixture into the prepared baking pan, taking care to bring the batter to the edges of the pan. Pour the pumpkin layer over it, leaving a little room at the edges if you can. Bake for ~{30%minutes}, until the pumpkin layer looks fairly firm (a little jiggling is okay) and has cracked at the edges a bit. 

Let the brownies cool for ~{20%minutes} and then transfer the pan to the fridge to set for at least ~{1.5%hours}. Once set, slice into wedges and serve. 

> A 15 or 16-ounce can of pumpkin will equal the amount of pumpkin needed for this recipe. 

> I had to bake these an extra 15 minutes. 

> I have tested this recipe with gluten-free baking flour and it turned out great. 